UID:0okvt3umia4quc1pau07javrn2@google.com
CREATED:20250709T204105Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>The Brad Meyer for Congress campaign is hosting a Roundtable
  Discussion on Universal Healthcare at the Bloomington Public Library on <s
 trong>July 26\, 2025 from 2-4 PM</strong>. One of the nation’s foremost adv
 ocates of “Medicare for All” – IU Assistant Professor of Medicine Robert C.
  Stone\, MD\, the Director and founder of Medicare for All Indiana – will l
 ead a panel of health care experts to explain the idea\, and they will answ
 er questions from the audience. SEATING IS LIMITED: you can reserve a seat 
 at the Brad Meyer for Congress website\, under the “Register for Event” tab
 . We will start giving seats away to walk-ins 5 minutes before the event st
 art\, so please don’t be late!  NO CHARGE OR CONTRIBUTION NEEDED! Come lear
 n about a progressive solution to Healthcare for all of Indiana and all of 
 America. </p><p> </p><p>Also\, we have a few folks lined up to help us with
  setup (1-2pm) and cleanup (4-5pm) for the event\, but we need several more
 ! Please volunteer at the “Contact Us” tab on the website. We are planning 
 many more events like this one\, and we need help to pull them off! </p><p>
 </p><p>Questions or suggestions can also be directed to the Contact Us page
 \, or to BobSchoumacher@gmail.com\, the Events Coordinator for the Brad Mey
 er for Congress campaign.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250709T204105Z
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library - Downtown\, 303 E Kirkwood Ave\, Blo
 omington\, IN 47408\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Brad Meyer for Congress Roundtable
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
